caption: Access and Facilities — Overview
technology-rule: overview

Separate character points from price, ownership, clinical access, law, and cultural reaction.

Money buys clinics, parts, licenses, maintenance, and faster service. Points pay for reliable personal capability. Legality Class, availability, registration, and cultural reaction are separate fields.

| Ownership Mode | Point Treatment | World Treatment | Can It Be Removed? |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Character Trait | Pay points. | Part of the character build. | Only by damage, surgery, or listed weakness. |
| Possession / Gear | Usually no points beyond gear traits. | Owned, issued, rented, or borrowed hardware. | Yes; can be stolen, recalled, or confiscated. |
| Hybrid - Recommended | Pay points and money/access. | Balanced permanent cyberwear. | Not casually, but it still needs repairs and service. |
| Point Debt | Receive the trait now; future points repay it. | Emergency surgery, patron reward, or story transformation. | Normally permanent once accepted. |

| Event | Suggested Point Debt |
| --- | --- |
| Minor practical implant | 1-10 points |
| Serious medical restoration | 5-25 points |
| Moderate performance upgrade | 10-50 points |
| Major combat suite | 50-100 points |
| Full conversion or chassis body | Agreed character arc and template |

| Access Tag | Meaning | Typical Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Common | Routine at the appropriate TL. | Biomonitor, basic medical prosthetic |
| Licensed | Requires registration, medical approval, or professional need. | Implant radio, industrial arm |
| Restricted | Controlled by government, corporation, guild, or temple. | Subdermal armor, combat chips, stealth ware |
| Military | Issued to armed services or approved champions. | Assault frames, hardpoints, tactical reflex systems |
| Illegal | Possession or concealment is criminal. | Poison injector, slave chip, unlicensed military weapon |
| Unique | Not normally sold; requires a patron, quest, or singular facility. | Divine limb, TL12 posthuman body, precursor relic |

| Cost Band | Typical TL9-Equivalent Price | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A - Minor | Under $1,000 | Small utility and diagnostic implants |
| B - Professional | $1,000-$10,000 | Datajacks, sensory upgrades, medical systems |
| C - Major | $10,000-$100,000 | Limbs, organs, chip slots, modest armor |
| D - Advanced | $100,000-$1,000,000 | Combat suites, power spines, radical neural systems |
| E - Conversion | $1,000,000-$10,000,000 | Chassis bodies, total conversion, major nanotech |
| F - Unique | No stable market price | Artifacts, divine work, TL12 miracles |

| LC | Classification | Typical Cybernetic Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| LC4 | Open | Biomonitor, ordinary medical prosthetic, passive tool implant, nonlethal utility system |
| LC3 | Licensed | Implant radio, encrypted datajack, industrial lift arm, ordinary cyberdeck, civilian full conversion |
| LC2 | Restricted | Subdermal armor, combat chips, reflex governor, stealth skin, surveillance implants |
| LC1 | Military | Combat frames, hardpoints, autonomous turrets, heavy integrated armor, military sensor suites |
| LC0 | Banned | Weapons of mass destruction, coercive slave systems, strategic antimatter or unrestricted disintegrator bodies |

| Field | Question It Answers | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Access Tag | Can the character find or commission it? | Unique divine limb |
| Legality Class | Who may lawfully possess it? | LC2 restricted armor |
| Registration | Must authorities know who has it? | Licensed implant radio |
| Concealment Rule | Is hiding it a separate offense? | Unregistered subdermal weapon |
| Social Reaction | How does the culture respond? | A feared but legal total cyborg |

| World Type | Restorative | Performance | Transformative | Unregistered / Hidden Weapons |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Corporate Cyberpunk City | Normal or positive | Normal if paid and registered | Status marker or corporate property | Strong legal penalty and tracking |
| Military Colony | Accepted | Respected if service-approved | Licensed specialist body | Treated as espionage or mutiny |
| Low-Tech Fantasy Kingdom | Miracle or unsettling | Feared as sorcery or golemcraft | Often treated as monster or divine sign | Execution, exorcism, or royal seizure |
| Cultivation Society | Accepted if harmonious | Viewed as external power unless chi-compatible | Sect-specific or spiritually suspect | Dishonorable or demonic |
| Post-Apocalyptic Mercenary State | Common among mercenaries | Often admired | Powerful but feared | Danger is expected more than legality |
| Humanitarian Reconstruction Facility | Supported when chosen and humane | Accepted with consent and ethical purpose | Evaluated for dignity and agency | Coercive systems and secret assassination ware condemned |
| Authoritarian Empire | Accepted when registered | Closely controlled | State property or weapon classification | Severe penalties and remote shutdown |

POINT DEBT

Use by agreement when an upgrade arrives before the character has enough unspent points. Future points pay the difference.
